@* Settings.razor — Phase 9 (user self-service Settings page)

   Route: /Settings. Linked from the sidebar's "Settings" item and the top
   bar's user-avatar click (both MainLayout.razor + Products.razor). Until
   now the sidebar entry existed but pointed at a route that 404'd — this
   page fills that gap.

   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   WHAT THE PAGE SHOWS
   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

   1. ACCOUNT CARD — read-only identity fields for the signed-in user:
        - Worker ID (login identifier)
        - Full name
        - Email (if present)
        - Gender (Male / Female, localized)
        - Active / Inactive status

      NOTE: Role information is deliberately NOT shown here. End users
      don't need to see their own role label (a customer shouldn't see
      "Customer" spelled out — it adds noise and can read as pejorative
      in some locales). Role awareness belongs on admin-side pages
      (UserManagement, UserDetail), not on a user's self-service page.

      Source: GetUserByIdQuery with the current user's Id. The query
      handler enforces that customers/read-only can ONLY query themselves
      (defense-in-depth — a Customer trying to query someone else's Id
      gets a "not found" error, same as UserDetail.razor's pattern).

   2. CHANGE PASSWORD button — navigates to /Account/ChangePassword,
      where the user can rotate their own password. We do NOT inline the
      change-password form here because that page is a STATIC SSR page
      (it has to re-issue the auth cookie on the same HTTP response, which
      a Blazor circuit can't do). Linking out is the correct pattern.

   3. APPEARANCE CARD — theme selector. Each available theme is rendered
      as a card button styled EXACTLY like the gender buttons in
      CreateUser.razor (RadzenCard with .usertype-option class, .is-selected
      for the active one, primary-tinted background + solid primary border
      when selected). Only one theme can be selected at a time. Clicking
      a theme:
        - calls window.takTheme.set(themeName) via JS interop (theme.js
          swaps the Radzen CSS <link> + layers the Tak override <link>).
        - updates _currentTheme so the clicked card immediately gets
          .is-selected and all the other cards lose it.
        - persists the choice in localStorage (theme.js does this for us).

      On page load, OnAfterRenderAsync(firstRender:true) reads
      window.takTheme.get() to find the saved theme and marks that card
      as selected. If JS interop fails (e.g. theme.js didn't load), the
      default `tak-light` is selected.

   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   ROLE RESOLUTION
   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Uses AuthenticationStateProvider (NOT ICurrentUserService.IsInRole)
   because in interactive Blazor Server mode, ICurrentUserService reads
   from IHttpContextAccessor.HttpContext which is null over the SignalR
   circuit. Same pattern as UserDetail.razor / ProductDetail.razor /
   Sales.razor. The user's Id is extracted from the "UserId" claim set
   by our custom IClaimsPrincipalFactory (with a fallback to
   ClaimTypes.NameIdentifier).

   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   THEME LIST — all themes the theme system can apply
   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   theme.js's TAK_THEMES registry only lists the CUSTOM Tak themes
   (tak-light, tak-dark) because those need a Radzen base + an override
   CSS file. But theme.js's applyTheme() function ALSO accepts ANY
   built-in Radzen theme name (standard, material, software, …) — when
   the name isn't in TAK_THEMES it just sets the Radzen <link> directly
   with no override. That means the user can switch to any Radzen theme
   too, not just the two Tak ones.

   We surface ALL of those themes here, grouped into two categories so
   the user can tell at a glance which is which:

     • Tak themes (2)        — tak-light, tak-dark. The project's custom
                               palette on top of a Radzen base. These are
                               the recommended defaults.
     • Radzen built-in (10) — default, dark, standard, standard-dark,
                               material, material-dark, software,
                               software-dark, humanistic, humanistic-dark.
                               Plain Radzen palettes with no Tak override.

   Adding a NEW Tak theme requires updating theme.js's TAK_THEMES AND
   the _availableThemes list below. Adding a NEW Radzen built-in only
   requires updating _availableThemes below — theme.js handles any
   unknown name by treating it as a Radzen base.

   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   LOCALIZATION
   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   All user-visible strings via IStringLocalizer<Settings> (Loc). Keys
   defined in Settings.en-US.resx + Settings.fa-IR.resx. RTL is handled
   at the <html dir> level by MainLayout.

   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   ANTIFORGERY
   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Not needed — no EditForm. All buttons are RadzenButton or RadzenCard
   with async Click handlers. The Blazor circuit's anti-forgery token is
   established at circuit start. No form POST happens. *@

@page "/Settings"
@attribute [Authorize]
@using System.Globalization
@using System.Security.Claims
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Authorization
@using Wolverine
@using TakOne.Application.Users.DTOs
@using TakOne.Application.Users.Queries.GetUserById
@using TakOne.Application.Notifications.DTOs
@using TakOne.Application.Notifications.Queries.GetNotificationPreferences
@using TakOne.Application.Notifications.Commands.SetNotificationMuted
@using TakOne.Domain.Notifications.Enums
@using TakOne.Domain.Users
@using TakOne.SharedKernel.Common
@using TakOne.WebUI.Services
@inject IMessageBus MessageBus
@inject AuthenticationStateProvider AuthStateProvider
@inject NavigationManager Navigation
@inject IStringLocalizer<Settings> Loc
@inject ToastService Toast
@inject IJSRuntime JS

<PageTitle>@Loc["PageTitle"]</PageTitle>

<HeadContent>
    <style>
            /* Layout — 12-col grid on desktop/tablet, stacks on mobile.
                                       Same shape as UserDetail.razor. */
            .settings-grid {
                display: grid;
                grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 2fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
                gap: 1.5rem;
                align-items: start;
            }

            @@media (max-width: 992px) {
                .settings-grid {
                    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
                    gap: 1rem;
                }
            }

            /* Page header — title + subtitle. */
            .settings-header {
                display: flex;
                align-items: center;
                gap: 0.75rem;
                margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
            }

                .settings-header .settings-title {
                    font-size: 1.6rem;
                    font-weight: 700;
                    margin: 0;
                    line-height: 1.2;
                }

            .settings-subtitle {
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                margin: 0 0 1rem 0;
                font-size: 0.9rem;
            }

            /* Account profile grid — 2-col label/value layout. Mirrors
                                       UserDetail.razor's .profile-grid so the two pages feel
                                       visually consistent. */
            .profile-grid {
                display: grid;
                grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 2fr);
                gap: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
                align-items: baseline;
            }

            @@media (max-width: 540px) {
                .profile-grid {
                    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
                    gap: 0.25rem 0;
                }
            }

            .profile-label {
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                font-size: 0.8125rem;
                font-weight: 500;
            }

            .profile-value {
                color: var(--rz-text-color);
                font-size: 0.9375rem;
                word-break: break-word;
            }

            .profile-value-mono {
                font-family: var(--rz-monospace-font-family, ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace);
            }

            .profile-value-muted {
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                font-style: italic;
            }

            /* Section card — title bar with icon. */
            .section-title {
                display: flex;
                align-items: center;
                gap: 0.5rem;
                font-weight: 600;
                margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
            }

            /* Theme selector — responsive auto-fill grid of card buttons.
                                       Mirrors CreateUser.razor's .usertype-toggle pattern exactly:
                                       each theme is a RadzenCard with the .usertype-option class;
                                       the selected theme's card additionally gets .is-selected.
                                       Selected = primary-tinted background + solid primary border.
                                       Unselected = outlined with the neutral border color.

                                       The grid uses auto-fill + minmax(170px, 1fr) so the cards
                                       wrap onto as many rows as needed. With 12 themes total
                                       (2 Tak + 10 Radzen built-in), this gives 4-6 columns on
                                       desktop, 2-3 on tablet, 1 on mobile — no overflow, no
                                       squashed cards. Each card has the theme's display name +
                                       a small sun/moon icon to hint at light vs dark. */
            .theme-toggle {
                display: grid;
                grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(170px, 1fr));
                gap: 0.75rem;
            }

            /* Category header — small all-caps label above each theme
                                       group ("Tak themes", "Radzen themes"). Visually groups the
                                       2 custom Tak themes apart from the 10 built-in Radzen ones
                                       so the user understands which is which at a glance. */
            .theme-category-header {
                font-size: 0.75rem;
                font-weight: 600;
                text-transform: uppercase;
                letter-spacing: 0.04em;
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                margin: 0.5rem 0 0.25rem 0;
            }

            /* .usertype-option is reused from CreateUser.razor. Re-declared
                                       here so this page is self-contained (CreateUser's CSS lives
                                       inside that page's scoped style block, not globally). */
            .usertype-option {
                transition: background-color 0.15s ease, border-color 0.15s ease;
            }

                .usertype-option.is-selected {
                    background-color: var(--rz-primary-lighter, rgba(var(--rz-primary-rgb, 67, 56, 202), 0.08));
                    border-color: var(--rz-primary) !important;
                }

            /* Theme card body — icon + name + hint stacked. */
            .theme-card-body {
                display: flex;
                flex-direction: column;
                gap: 0.35rem;
                text-align: center;
            }

            .theme-card-name {
                font-weight: 600;
                margin: 0;
            }

            .theme-card-hint {
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                font-size: 0.75rem;
                margin: 0;
            }

            /* Action row — the "Change password" button + spacer. */
            .action-row {
                display: flex;
                gap: 0.75rem;
                flex-wrap: wrap;
                margin-top: 0.75rem;
            }

            /* ── Notification preferences card (Round 3) ─────────────
               One row per NotificationKind: leading icon in a tinted
               squircle (same visual family as the Notifications page's
               .notif-icon), kind label + short description, and a
               RadzenSwitch on the trailing edge. Rows separate with a
               hairline so the list reads as a table without being one. */
            .notif-prefs-list {
                display: flex;
                flex-direction: column;
                margin-top: 0.75rem;
            }

            .notif-pref-row {
                display: flex;
                align-items: center;
                gap: 0.85rem;
                padding: 0.6rem 0.25rem;
                border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rz-border-color);
            }

            .notif-pref-row:last-child {
                border-bottom: none;
            }

            .notif-pref-icon {
                display: flex;
                align-items: center;
                justify-content: center;
                width: 2.35rem;
                height: 2.35rem;
                border-radius: 10px;
                flex: none;
                background: var(--rz-secondary-background-color, var(--rz-base-background-color));
                color: var(--rz-primary);
            }

            .notif-pref-text {
                flex: 1;
                min-width: 0;
            }

            .notif-pref-name {
                font-weight: 600;
                font-size: 0.9rem;
            }

            .notif-pref-desc {
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                font-size: 0.75rem;
                line-height: 1.35;
            }

            .notif-pref-hint {
                margin-top: 0.6rem;
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                font-size: 0.78rem;
                line-height: 1.5;
            }

            /* Loading + error + not-found states reuse Radzen's alert
                                       components — same pattern as ProductDetail.razor. */
    </style>
</HeadContent>

<RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Vertical" Gap="1rem">
    @* ── Page header ── *@
    <div>
        <div class="settings-header">
            <RadzenIcon Icon="settings" Style="font-size: 1.75rem; color: var(--rz-primary);" />
            <h1 class="settings-title">@Loc["PageHeading"]</h1>
        </div>
        <p class="settings-subtitle">@Loc["PageSubheading"]</p>
    </div>

    @* ── Loading state ── *@
    @if (_isLoading)
    {
        <RadzenCard>
            <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal" AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Gap="0.75rem">
                <RadzenProgressBarCircular ShowValue="false" Mode="ProgressBarMode.Indeterminate" Size="ProgressBarCircularSize.Medium" />
                <RadzenText Text="@Loc["Loading"]" TextStyle="TextStyle.Body1" />
            </RadzenStack>
        </RadzenCard>
    }

    @* ── Error state ── *@
    else if (_loadError is not null)
    {
        <RadzenAlert Title="@Loc["ErrorTitle"]"
                     Text="@_loadError"
                     AlertStyle="AlertStyle.Danger"
                     Variant="Variant.Filled"
                     ShowIcon="true" />
    }

    @* ── Main content ── *@
    else if (_user is not null)
    {
        <div class="settings-grid">
            @* LEFT — account + appearance cards *@
            <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Vertical" Gap="1rem">
                @* ── Account card — read-only identity fields ── *@
                <RadzenCard Variant="Variant.Filled" Style="padding: 1.5rem;">
                    <div class="section-title">
                        <RadzenIcon Icon="person" Style="color: var(--rz-primary);" />
                        <span>@Loc["AccountCardTitle"]</span>
                    </div>

                    <div class="profile-grid">
                        <div class="profile-label">@Loc["ColWorkerId"]</div>
                        <div class="profile-value profile-value-mono">@(CultureFormat.FormatDigits(_user.WorkerId))</div>

                        <div class="profile-label">@Loc["ColFullName"]</div>
                        <div class="profile-value">@_user.FullName</div>

                        <div class="profile-label">@Loc["ColGender"]</div>
                        <div class="profile-value">@GetGenderLabel(_user.Gender)</div>

                        @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_user.Email))
                        {
                            <div class="profile-label">@Loc["ColEmail"]</div>
                            <div class="profile-value profile-value-mono">@_user.Email</div>
                        }

                        <div class="profile-label">@Loc["ColStatus"]</div>
                        <div class="profile-value">
                            @if (_user.IsActive)
                            {
                                <RadzenBadge Text="@Loc["StatusActive"]" BadgeStyle="BadgeStyle.Success" IsPill="true" />
                            }
                            else
                            {
                                <RadzenBadge Text="@Loc["StatusInactive"]" BadgeStyle="BadgeStyle.Light" IsPill="true" />
                            }
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    @* Change password button — links out to /Account/ChangePassword.
                       That page is a STATIC SSR page (not interactive) because it
                       has to re-issue the auth cookie on the same HTTP response.
                       We can't inline its form here. forceLoad:true is REQUIRED —
                       navigating from an interactive circuit to a static SSR page
                       without a full HTTP reload leaves the circuit alive and the
                       static page never renders. *@
                    <div class="action-row">
                        <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["ChangePassword"]"
                                      Icon="lock_reset"
                                      ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Primary"
                                      Variant="Variant.Filled"
                                      Click="@(() => Navigation.NavigateTo("/Account/ChangePassword", forceLoad: true))" />
                    </div>
                </RadzenCard>

                @* ── Appearance card — theme selector ──
                   Renders one RadzenCard per available theme, styled exactly
                   like the gender buttons in CreateUser.razor (same .usertype-option
                   class + .is-selected modifier). Only the active theme's card
                   has .is-selected, so only one card shows the primary-tinted
                   background + solid primary border at a time. Clicking a card
                   calls window.takTheme.set(themeName) via JS interop and
                   updates _currentTheme to re-render the list.

                   The themes are grouped into two categories, each rendered
                   under a small all-caps header so the user can tell the
                   custom Tak themes apart from the built-in Radzen ones:
                     1. "Tak themes"        — tak-light, tak-dark
                     2. "Radzen themes"    — default, dark, standard, …
                   Both groups share the SAME .theme-toggle grid + .usertype-option
                   card style — the grouping is purely visual. *@
                <RadzenCard Variant="Variant.Filled" Style="padding: 1.5rem;">
                    <div class="section-title">
                        <RadzenIcon Icon="palette" Style="color: var(--rz-primary);" />
                        <span>@Loc["AppearanceCardTitle"]</span>
                    </div>

                    <RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Body2"
                                Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color); display: block; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
                        @Loc["ThemeHint"]
                    </RadzenText>

                    @* Render each category group with its own header. We
                       iterate over _themeCategories so the order + grouping
                       is data-driven (not hard-coded in markup). Adding a
                       new category only requires editing _availableThemes +
                       _themeCategories — the markup stays the same. *@
                    @foreach (var category in _themeCategories)
                    {
                        <p class="theme-category-header">@GetCategoryHeader(category)</p>
                        <div class="theme-toggle">
                            @foreach (var theme in _availableThemes.Where(t => t.Category == category.Id))
                            {
                                var themeId = theme.Id; // closure capture for the lambda
                                var isSelected = _currentTheme == themeId;
                                <RadzenCard Variant="@(isSelected ? Variant.Filled : Variant.Outlined)"
                                            Class="@GetToggleClass(isSelected)"
                                            Style="@GetToggleBorderStyle(isSelected)"
                                            @onclick="@(() => HandleSelectThemeAsync(themeId))">
                                    <div class="theme-card-body">
                                        <RadzenIcon Icon="@theme.Icon"
                                                    Style="@GetToggleIconStyle(isSelected)" />
                                        <RadzenText Text="@GetThemeName(themeId)"
                                                    TextStyle="TextStyle.Subtitle1"
                                                    Style="@GetToggleTextStyle(isSelected)" />
                                        <RadzenText Text="@GetThemeHint(themeId)"
                                                    TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption"
                                                    Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color); margin: 0;" />
                                    </div>
                                </RadzenCard>
                            }
                        </div>
                    }

                    @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(_themeToast))
                    {
                        <RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption"
                                    Style="color: var(--rz-success, #16a34a); display: block; margin-top: 0.5rem;">
                            @_themeToast
                        </RadzenText>
                    }
                </RadzenCard>
            </RadzenStack>

            @* RIGHT — notification preferences card (Round 3 feature:
               per-user, per-kind mute flags enforced at notification
               creation time), then help / about cards. *@
            <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Vertical" Gap="1rem">
                <RadzenCard Variant="Variant.Outlined" Style="padding: 1.25rem;">
                    <div class="section-title">
                        <RadzenIcon Icon="notifications" Style="color: var(--rz-primary);" />
                        <span>@Loc["NotifPrefsCardTitle"]</span>
                    </div>
                    @if (_prefsLoadError is not null)
                    {
                        <RadzenAlert Title="@Loc["ErrorTitle"]"
                                     Text="@_prefsLoadError"
                                     AlertStyle="AlertStyle.Danger"
                                     Variant="Variant.Filled"
                                     ShowIcon="true"
                                     Style="margin-top: 0.75rem;" />
                    }
                    else if (_notificationPreferences is null)
                    {
                        <div class="tm-skel-stack" aria-busy="true" aria-live="polite" style="margin-top: 0.75rem;">
                            @for (var i = 0; i < 4; i++)
                            {
                                <div class="tm-skel-row">
                                    <div class="tm-skel tm-skel--thumb"></div>
                                    <div class="tm-skel-stack" style="gap:.4rem; flex:1;">
                                        <div class="tm-skel tm-skel--line"></div>
                                        <div class="tm-skel tm-skel--line tm-skel--w60"></div>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="tm-skel tm-skel--chip"></div>
                                </div>
                            }
                        </div>
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        <div class="notif-prefs-list">
                            @foreach (var pref in _notificationPreferences)
                            {
                                <div class="notif-pref-row">
                                    <div class="notif-pref-icon">
                                        <RadzenIcon Icon="@GetNotifPrefIcon(pref.Kind)" />
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="notif-pref-text">
                                        <div class="notif-pref-name">@GetNotifPrefName(pref.Kind)</div>
                                        <div class="notif-pref-desc">@GetNotifPrefDesc(pref.Kind)</div>
                                    </div>
                                    <RadzenSwitch TValue="bool"
                                                  Value="@pref.IsMuted"
                                                  Disabled="@_isSavingPref"
                                                  Name="@($"pref-switch-{(int)pref.Kind}")"
                                                  Change="@(async value => await HandleNotifPrefToggleAsync(pref.Kind, value))" />
                                </div>
                            }
                        </div>
                        <p class="notif-pref-hint">@Loc["NotifPrefsHint"]</p>
                    }
                </RadzenCard>

                <RadzenCard Variant="Variant.Outlined" Style="padding: 1.25rem;">
                    <div class="section-title">
                        <RadzenIcon Icon="help_outline" Style="color: var(--rz-primary);" />
                        <span>@Loc["HelpCardTitle"]</span>
                    </div>
                    <RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Body2"
                                Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color); line-height: 1.6;">
                        @Loc["HelpCardText"]
                    </RadzenText>
                </RadzenCard>

                <RadzenCard Variant="Variant.Outlined" Style="padding: 1.25rem;">
                    <div class="section-title">
                        <RadzenIcon Icon="info" Style="color: var(--rz-primary);" />
                        <span>@Loc["AboutCardTitle"]</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="profile-grid">
                        <div class="profile-label">@Loc["ColApp"]</div>
                        <div class="profile-value">TakOne</div>
                    </div>
                </RadzenCard>
            </RadzenStack>
        </div>
    }
</RadzenStack>

@code {
    // ── State ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private UserDto? _user;
    private string? _loadError;
    private bool _isLoading = true;

    /// <summary>
    /// The user's per-kind notification preferences (Round 3). Null while
    /// loading / on load failure (the card renders its skeleton / error
    /// state respectively). One entry per NotificationKind — the query
    /// guarantees the complete list.
    /// </summary>
    private List<NotificationPreferenceDto>? _notificationPreferences;

    /// <summary>
    /// Non-null when the preferences query failed — the card renders an
    /// inline RadzenAlert instead of the list (the rest of the page still
    /// works; account + theme are loaded independently).
    /// </summary>
    private string? _prefsLoadError;

    /// <summary>
    /// True while a SetNotificationMutedCommand is in flight — disables
    /// ALL the switches (prevents stacking a second toggle on a
    /// first-in-flight one; the upsert's race-loser path would surface a
    /// confusing error toast for a double-click).
    /// </summary>
    private bool _isSavingPref;

    /// <summary>
    /// The currently-applied theme name. Initialized to "tak-light" (the
    /// project default) and then synced with theme.js's saved value in
    /// OnAfterRenderAsync(firstRender:true) — same pattern as MainLayout.razor.
    /// Drives the .is-selected class on the theme cards.
    /// </summary>
    private string _currentTheme = "tak-light";

    /// <summary>
    /// Transient "theme applied" toast — shown briefly after a theme
    /// switch so the user gets feedback that the click was registered.
    /// Cleared on the next switch. Kept as a simple string (not a
    /// ToastService call) so it persists alongside the card.
    /// </summary>
    private string? _themeToast;

    /// <summary>
    /// One entry per available theme. The Id matches the keys in theme.js's
    /// TAK_THEMES registry (for Tak themes) OR a built-in Radzen theme name
    /// (for Radzen themes). Adding a new theme requires updating this list;
    /// for Tak themes you ALSO need to update theme.js's TAK_THEMES.
    ///
    /// The Icon is a Material Symbols name (light_mode for light themes,
    /// dark_mode for dark themes) — rendered via RadzenIcon.
    ///
    /// NameKey + HintKey are resx keys (looked up via Loc[...]) — they
    /// decouple the display strings from the theme Id so the Id can stay
    /// stable (e.g. "tak-light") while the user-visible name can be
    /// localized ("Tak Light" / "پوسته روشن").
    ///
    /// Category groups the theme under a header in the UI ("Tak themes"
    /// vs "Radzen themes") — must match a ThemeCategory.Id in
    /// _themeCategories below.
    /// </summary>
    private readonly List<ThemeOption> _availableThemes = new()
    {
        // ── Tak themes (custom palette on top of a Radzen base) ──
        // These are the project's recommended defaults. The override CSS
        // files (tak-light.css, tak-dark.css) live in wwwroot/css/Themes/.
        new ThemeOption("tak-light",       "light_mode", IsDark: false,
            NameKey: "ThemeName_TakLight",       HintKey: "ThemeHint_TakLight",       Category: "Tak"),
        new ThemeOption("tak-dark",        "dark_mode",  IsDark: true,
            NameKey: "ThemeName_TakDark",        HintKey: "ThemeHint_TakDark",        Category: "Tak"),

        // ── Radzen built-in themes (no Tak override) ──
        // theme.js's applyTheme() handles any unknown theme name by
        // treating it as a Radzen base — so all of these work without
        // any registry changes in theme.js.
        new ThemeOption("standard",        "light_mode", IsDark: false,
